    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d1126f77_a5538a75",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 2146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1269501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-12T23:25:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Checking: we\u0027re all synced on Type-C R2.0 August 2019, correct?\n\nAseda and I investigated this at length, whether a DebugSNK PR_SWAP is allowed. True, state jump arrow isn\u0027t on state diagram \"Figure 4-16 Connection State Diagram: DRP with Accessory and Try.SRC Support\". But I think it is merely an accidental omission in the spec.\n\nI believe PR_SWAP in \"DebugAccessory.SNK\" should go to \" UnorientedDebugAccessory.SRC\". Just as \"Attached.SNK\" goes to \"AttachWait.SRC\".\n\nPlease see crbug/1023077 for the \"Oriented\" state.",
      "parentUuid": "7ec71bf1_69093f48",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2138,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 2146,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "b479247fdc3e27d68aa7fec47b1e82fbeb678181",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0f608a10_50e5a0dd",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 2146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1269501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-13T03:23:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just spoke with one of the writers of the Type-C/PD specifications, David S.\n\nI was informed we are allowed to do pretty much anything we want in Debug mode, repurpose pins, etc. So I believe we are fully within our rights to enable a PR_SWAP jump to/from DrbugSNK and UnorientedDebugSRC states as described above -- mirroring AttachedSRC and AttachedSNK PR_SWAP jump.\n\nHe also confirmed are not currently implementing OrientedDebugSRC state due to CCD not having polarity support (for various reasons including reliability), but leaves that open as a possibility in the future.\n\nTL;DR: We should continue to allow PR_SWAP here for ServoV4.",
      "parentUuid": "d1126f77_a5538a75",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2138,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 2146,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "b479247fdc3e27d68aa7fec47b1e82fbeb678181",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
